## 1. Objective restatement and acceptance surface (traceability)

Land the completed extraction probe at `reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md`: for each
of three real sealed goals (B0.0, B0.1, B0.2), a hand-extraction into the SAEOS-1 §4.3 node
types scored per-field extractable / partial / absent, with an explicit GO or NO-GO verdict and
the loss ratio. The sealed artifact satisfies this in full: **126 slots scored across 3 goals,
`verdict: GO`, `loss_ratio: 0.25`.**

The gate is four assertions, run from the repo root. They are the acceptance oracle and are
reproduced **verbatim** — do not alter one character:

```
A1  test -f reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
A2  rg -q '^verdict: (GO|NO-GO)$' reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
A3  test $(rg -c '^## goal: ' reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md) -ge 3
A4  rg -q '^loss_ratio: 0\.[0-9]+$' reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
```

**Assertion-fragility analysis (load-bearing — read before editing the deliverable).**

| # | Satisfied by | Fragility the BUILDER must not introduce |
|---|---|---|
| A1 | the file at exactly that path | `reviews/spikes/` already exists (holds `DEBT-0002-spawnability-spike.md`), so no directory creation is needed; a path typo is the only realistic failure |
| A2 | `verdict: GO` at the artifact's header **and** again in §5 | `^…$` anchors: **any** trailing whitespace, leading indent, or wrapping the line inside a fenced code block breaks the match |
| A3 | exactly three `## goal: B0.x — …` headings | requires literal `## goal: ` with **one** space after the colon; `-ge 3` is a floor, so adding goals is safe, renaming or re-casing the heading is not |
| A4 | `loss_ratio: 0.25` at the header | the three `goal_loss_ratio: 0.35 / 0.17 / 0.23` lines **must not** match, and do not, solely because of the `^` anchor. **Do not rename `goal_loss_ratio` to end in a bare `loss_ratio` at line start** — it would still pass, but it would make A4 ambiguous about which number the gate read |

**A3 failure-mode hazard.** On zero matches `rg -c` prints nothing and exits 1, so A3 degrades
to `test  -ge 3` — a shell *syntax error*, not a clean FAIL. VERIFIER must therefore run A1
first and report A3's raw count separately (§3, E2), so "file absent", "heading malformed" and
"too few goals" are distinguishable rather than collapsing into one uninterpretable error.

**Ignore-rules check (cleared).** `rg` honours `.gitignore`, but the repo `.gitignore` excludes
only `.DS_Store`, `node_modules/`, `*.log`, `.scratch/`, `.runtime/`, `.venv/`, `__pycache__/`,
`*.py[cod]`, `.pytest_cache/`, `.ruff_cache/` and `ops/keys/*` — `reviews/` is not excluded, and
